<!-- Menu in the IG's DEFAULT language (English).
     The IG Publisher renders the navigation from this file. To translate it,
     ship a per-language copy at input/translations/<lang>/includes/menu.xml —
     this is the mechanism the HL7 reference IG FHIR/multi-lang-test-ig uses and
     the ONLY way to get a TRANSLATED menu: the `menu:` property in
     sushi-config.yaml generates a single menu.xml that cannot be translated.
     Rules: keep the href targets identical across languages; dropdown parents
     must link to a REAL page (href="#" is rejected by the template's menu QA);
     only one sub-menu level is supported.

     STRUCTURE: this implements the TF-KDS-agreed module menu of
     mii-kds-module-template (v0.11.1 / v0.13.2 — identical), plus the entries
     for this module's own pages. Deviations from the scaffold menu, all of them
     additions rather than changes:
     - Guidance carries four module-own pages (Terminology, Laboratory
       Timestamps, Project Context, References).
     - Artifacts carries the four per-resource profile pages after Profiles.
       They are one level deep because only one sub-menu level is supported.
     - Translations is a top-level entry: this IG is bilingual, the page exists,
       and every narrative page must be reachable from a menu.
     Optional (0..1) pages the module does NOT have — Search Parameters,
     Operations, Code Systems — are absent by decision: the module defines no
     SearchParameter, no OperationDefinition and no CodeSystem resources.

     LINK-ONLY ENTRIES (no page of their own):
     - "Datasets and Descriptions" points at the Logical Models page — the
       module's datasets ARE its logical models.
     - The four Conformance entries point at the KDS-wide conformance rules of
       the Meta module. INTERIM: the Meta module has no published IG rendering
       yet, so these link to the authoritative meta-wiki sections; switch them
       to the Meta IG's menu entries once a stable rendering exists. -->
